{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1025657-ideas-tips-and-builds-for-a-new-vampire-character","id":1025657,"title":"Ideas, Tips, and Builds for a New Vampire character","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-02T18:17:58-08:00","id":1025657,"title":"Ideas, Tips, and Builds for a New Vampire character","content":"I've been apart of a Vampire game now for about a year, and finally my character went down. Nothing glorious either, I merely misjudged a situation and was torn apart by those Carthian Bastards. Regardless, i'm looking for some tips and help onto my new character build, which I am making a kind of Vampire Mad Doctor or Scientist. I plan to be starting Carthian for Night Doctor, but will eventually take into the Ordo Dracul<br /> <br /> This character is supposed to be the type who captures people, and in the great name of medical science does horrendous, and obviously void of any ethical value. It's being my approach to being one of the more, whats he doing at the sides, and I love the concepts of the mad experimenter or scientist (Especially after my recent completion of the amnesia games.)<br /> <br /> So if anyone here has tips, ideas or even builds I would be appreciative. Character has 30xp start and due to the volitale Nature of London and in no small part to a resident Jackass, clans are limited with Nos, Gangrel, and Daeva being the only avaliables to be sired from. Though I see anyone of them could help with the idea of a monstrous doctor, or savage butcher, or the smooth talking psycho. <br /> <br /> Always remember to see your Doctors","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11595-chaos965","name":"Chaos965","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11595_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T18:50:10-08:00","id":1025669,"title":"","content":"If it's set in London, you can't go wrong having a character concept who worked as an administrator or inmate here. <a href=\"https://historicengland.org.uk/research/inclusive-heritage/disability-history/1050-1485/from-bethlehem-to-bedlam/\" target=\"_blank\">https://historicengland.org.uk/resea...hem-to-bedlam/</a> The place was a medical hospital, poorhouse, prison, and insane asylum and the subject of many political, religious, and medical scandals over the centuries. <br /> <br /> The Nosferatu bloodline Morotrophians is one of the few bloodlines I liked personally and certainly fit in the concept you are considering.<br /> <br /> Some of the practices of Dr. Thredson or Dr. Arden in season 2 of American Horror Story might be good for mining ideas of unethical practices that are serve dubious beneficial medicinal or psychiatric value. Or you could do a bit of research on real life serial killers who held medical degrees like H. H. Holmes or Harold Shipman.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}